#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:1
#: d42d360c171241268ff757a1364811a3
msgid "Environmental Directional Distance: Producing More with Less Pollution"
msgstr "环境方向性距离：以更少污染生产更多产出"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:3
#: 1294ea2615214ea2a264ddaf15361c7c
msgid ""
"A power company is rarely asked simply to “be efficient.” It may be asked to"
" supply more electricity while lowering carbon emissions. A hospital may "
"need to treat more patients without increasing hazardous waste. A farm may "
"want to maintain food output while reducing nutrient losses. In each case, "
"managers face a joint operating programme: improve the service the "
"organization exists to provide and reduce the residual society would prefer "
"to avoid."
msgstr "电力公司很少只被要求“提高效率”，更常见的目标是在降低碳排放的同时提供更多电力。医院可能需要在不增加危险废物的情况下诊疗更多患者；农场可能希望在维持粮食产出的同时减少养分流失。每种情形中，管理者都面对一套联合经营方案：改善组织本应提供的服务，同时减少社会希望避免的残余物。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:10
#: 8d8d19ea7aa845e6b3ef8341aa42c560
msgid ""
"An ordinary output-oriented DEA model cannot express that programme. If "
"emissions are entered as an ordinary output, producing more of them looks "
"favourable. If they are entered as an input, they are treated as a resource "
"committed before production, much like labour or capital. Environmental DEA "
"instead recognizes undesirable outputs as consequences produced jointly with"
" useful activity. It asks how far service expansion and burden reduction can"
" proceed together, given what the study assumes about abatement, foregone "
"output, and the operating practices observed in the comparison population."
msgstr ""
"普通产出导向 DEA "
"无法表达这套方案。若把排放作为普通产出，模型会把更多排放视为有利；若把它作为投入，则相当于把排放当成生产前已经承诺的资源，与劳动或资本相似。环境 DEA"
" 把非合意产出视为与有用活动联合产生的后果，并在研究对治理、产出牺牲和比较总体经营实践作出假设后，考察服务扩张与负担削减能够共同推进多远。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:19
#: 80262c315dc64287bf1c554fba9ff5a6
msgid "Pollution is part of the production account"
msgstr "污染是生产账户的一部分"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:21
#: 53bc45f78295413dbf7be4a5301d826f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Let $x\\in\\mathbb{R}^m_+$ denote inputs, $y\\in\\mathbb{R}^s_+$ desirable "
"outputs, and $b\\in\\mathbb{R}^q_+$ undesirable outputs. The environmental "
"technology is"
msgstr ""
"令 $x\\in\\mathbb{R}^m_+$ 表示投入，$y\\in\\mathbb{R}^s_+$ "
"表示合意产出，$b\\in\\mathbb{R}^q_+$ 表示非合意产出。环境技术为"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:24
#: 103c6618fc824487958768cd4c2dbe71
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T\n"
"=\\{(x,y,b):x\\text{ can jointly produce }(y,b)\\}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T\n"
"=\\{(x,y,b):x\\text{ 可联合生产 }(y,b)\\}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:29
#: e07d02fae27a4c1081ec9d0de7ffcded
msgid "For a fixed resource commitment, the feasible output set is"
msgstr "给定资源承诺时，可行产出集为"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:31
#: aa44da79eb204262a5058d6f8192f286
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"P(x)=\\{(y,b):(x,y,b)\\in\\mathcal T\\}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"P(x)=\\{(y,b):(x,y,b)\\in\\mathcal T\\}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:35
#: a08bf9bfde574cdb8c506da3248a3a9b
msgid ""
"The word *jointly* carries the economics. Electricity and emissions are not "
"two unrelated products placed in the same table. They arise from an "
"operating process, and reducing emissions may require cleaner fuel, "
"abatement activity, lost output, or a different production plan. The "
"technology must say which of these possibilities the benchmark comparison is"
" allowed to represent."
msgstr "“联合”一词承载着经济含义。电力和排放不是碰巧放在同一张表中的两个无关产品，而是由同一经营过程产生；减少排放可能需要更清洁燃料、治理活动、牺牲产出或改变生产方案。技术必须说明标杆比较允许表示其中哪些可能性。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:41
#: 6a6876b7445c45a4b81f33cea700688d
msgid "Weak and strong disposal answer different economic questions"
msgstr "弱可处置性与强可处置性回答不同的经济问题"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:43
#: a9de31dcfc5d4e10b349ca22f9977bfa
msgid ""
"The first management question is whether pollution can be reduced "
"independently while useful output and the represented resource commitment "
"are preserved, or whether lowering pollution requires curtailing the joint "
"production activity unless a cleaner process is represented. Weak "
"disposability adopts the latter view. If $(y,b)\\in P(x)$, then"
msgstr ""
"第一个管理问题是：污染能否在保留有用产出和所代表资源承诺时独立减少，还是在没有更清洁过程进入参照技术时，污染削减必须伴随联合生产活动收缩。弱可处置性采用后一种观点。若"
" $(y,b)\\in P(x)$，则"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:49
#: dc271bf9a4b04462800f314710742f65
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"(\\alpha y,\\alpha b)\\in P(x)\n"
"\\qquad\\text{for}\\qquad 0\\leq\\alpha\\leq1.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"(\\alpha y,\\alpha b)\\in P(x)\n"
"\\qquad\\text{对于}\\qquad 0\\leq\\alpha\\leq1.\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:54
#: 7524839642e24ad1b24469ecc30e79e6
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Undesirable output cannot simply be deleted while everything else is held "
"unchanged. Reducing it is represented as requiring some sacrifice or "
"adjustment in the joint production plan. This is a natural baseline when "
"pollution control uses resources or constrains desirable output. Chung, "
"Färe, and Grosskopf combined this production assumption with a directional "
"distance function to study environmental productivity {cite:p}`chung1997`."
msgstr ""
"非合意产出不能在其他条件不变时被直接删除。模型把污染削减表示为需要联合生产方案作出某种牺牲或调整。当污染控制消耗资源或约束合意产出时，这是自然的基准假设。Chung、Färe"
" 和 Grosskopf 将这一生产假设与方向性距离函数结合，用于研究环境生产率 {cite:p}`chung1997`。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:61
#: 1adec0764a8c42dfb5edb5702b2290ef
msgid ""
"Here *costly* describes a restriction on the production opportunities "
"represented by the model. It does not measure a monetary abatement cost, an "
"engineering treatment cost, or the causal effect of environmental "
"regulation."
msgstr "这里的“有成本”描述模型所代表生产机会受到的限制，不是货币治理成本、工程处理成本或环境监管因果效应的测量。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:65
#: 42f69a1fe7bc40c58a3ae6c21d00114d
msgid ""
"Strong disposability instead allows a plan with no more pollution than the "
"observed plan to be used as a comparator without recording an accompanying "
"sacrifice. In a classic CRS common-factor joint-envelopment account such as "
"the one used below, the distinction appears in the bad-output restriction:"
msgstr "强可处置性则允许把污染不高于观测方案的活动作为比较对象，而不记录伴随牺牲。在下文采用的经典 CRS 共同因子联合包络账户中，二者区别体现在非合意产出约束："

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:70
#: 7fca910fb2404da3aedb77fe58c6ddc7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"B\\lambda=b\n"
"\\quad\\text{under common-factor weak disposal},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"B\\lambda\\leq b\n"
"\\quad\\text{under its strong-disposal counterpart}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"B\\lambda=b\n"
"\\quad\\text{在共同因子弱处置下},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"B\\lambda\\leq b\n"
"\\quad\\text{在相应强处置下}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:78
#: aa04e90dbdfc4b788f77ea4a266bf287
msgid ""
"Strong disposal may be defensible when pollution-control resources and "
"treatment activities are already measured, or useful as a sensitivity "
"benchmark. It does not show that removal is costless in money or engineering"
" terms. It says that the model requires no loss of useful output when the "
"residual falls. If abatement consumes unmeasured resources, this assumption "
"can overstate the environmental improvement available to managers and "
"regulators."
msgstr "当污染控制资源和处理活动已经纳入测量时，强可处置性可能合理，也可作为敏感性标杆。它不表示治理在货币或工程意义上没有成本，只表示残余物减少时模型不要求有用产出随之损失。若治理消耗了未测量资源，该假设可能夸大管理者和监管者可用的环境改进机会。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:85
#: 01d8f7d607d942579f152bf5b08d94dd
msgid ""
"Weak disposability contracts desirable and undesirable outputs together, "
"whereas the strong-disposal account records no accompanying sacrifice when "
"undesirable output falls while desirable output is fixed"
msgstr "弱可处置性使合意产出与非合意产出共同收缩；强可处置账户则在合意产出固定、非合意产出下降时不记录伴随牺牲"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:90
#: 734f270939d94479b9ebb66a83de1000
msgid ""
"The disposal assumption changes the managerial opportunity set. Weak "
"disposal treats pollution reduction as costly within the production account;"
" the strong-disposal account does not represent an accompanying loss of "
"desirable output."
msgstr "处置性假设改变管理机会集。弱可处置性在生产账户内把污染削减视为有成本；强可处置账户不表示合意产出需要伴随下降。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:95
#: 77686c59c2a64e8ca23330c203e28516
msgid "Null jointness is a separate assumption:"
msgstr "零结合性是另一项独立假设："

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:97
#: 34bf83d235c54c3090802d3c18edac4a
msgid ""
"\n"
"b=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=0.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"b=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=0.\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:101
#: dbda8ebaadc04bfd95b81e5d60218b51
msgid ""
"It says that the modeled desirable output cannot be produced without "
"generating some of the residual. That may be reasonable for an unavoidable "
"by-product of combustion, but not for a sample containing verified zero-"
"emission production, complete capture, or recycling. Weak disposability and "
"null jointness should therefore be defended from the production process, not"
" adopted merely because the variable is called pollution. In the technology "
"used here, null jointness belongs to the weak-disposal account; it cannot be"
" combined coherently with strong disposal, which permits the residual to be "
"reduced independently in the represented opportunity set."
msgstr "它表示所建模的合意产出不能在完全没有相应残余物时生产。对燃烧不可避免的副产物而言，这可能合理；若样本包含经核实的零排放生产、完全捕集或回收，则未必合理。因此，弱可处置性和零结合性必须依据生产过程辩护，不能只因为变量名是污染就直接采用。在本章技术中，零结合性属于弱可处置账户；它不能与强可处置性连贯结合，因为后者允许在所代表机会集中独立减少残余物。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:110
#: 67a2b2ee46f844b999da9ceeee604877
msgid "Weak disposal still leaves a benchmarking choice"
msgstr "弱可处置性仍然留下标杆构造选择"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:112
#: e8c848e39a814768b011e2bc22b21ea0
msgid ""
"The weak-disposal axiom does not by itself determine how observed "
"organizations may be combined. In the classic constant-returns construction,"
" one common activity account represents the benchmark:"
msgstr "弱可处置公理本身不决定如何组合观测组织。在经典规模报酬不变构造中，一个共同活动账户表示标杆："

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:116
#: fa88959f929a4bb8b6e88e979ac9b655
msgid ""
"\n"
"X\\lambda\\leq x,\\qquad\n"
"Y\\lambda\\geq y,\\qquad\n"
"B\\lambda=b,\\qquad\n"
"\\lambda\\geq0.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"X\\lambda\\leq x,\\qquad\n"
"Y\\lambda\\geq y,\\qquad\n"
"B\\lambda=b,\\qquad\n"
"\\lambda\\geq0.\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:123
#: 616bc43025354e9db6a8f1615650e873
msgid ""
"Because activity can be scaled under constant returns, the represented "
"desirable and undesirable outputs can be curtailed together. Economically, "
"the benchmark applies a common proportional adjustment to the whole "
"reference production portfolio. That common-factor interpretation relies on "
"CRS: simply adding a VRS convexity restriction to $B\\lambda=b$ does not "
"create an identified VRS weak-disposal technology."
msgstr ""
"规模报酬不变允许活动按比例缩放，因此所代表的合意产出与非合意产出可以共同收缩。从经济上看，标杆对整个参照生产组合采用共同的比例调整。该共同因子解释依赖 "
"CRS：仅向 $B\\lambda=b$ 增加 VRS 凸性约束，不能产生已识别的 VRS 弱可处置技术。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:129
#: e02613eede054deea511352173dd7324
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Under VRS, a source-qualified alternative lets the reference activities "
"carry different retention rates {cite:p}`kuosmanen2005`. DEAPack represents "
"each activity by an active part $\\mu_j$, which contributes desirable and "
"undesirable outputs, and a curtailed part $\\eta_j$, which still belongs to "
"the input portfolio. Convexity applies to the full activity account,"
msgstr ""
"在 VRS 下，一项具有来源依据的替代方案允许各参照活动具有不同保留率 {cite:p}`kuosmanen2005`。DEAPack 用活跃部分 "
"$\\mu_j$ 表示每项活动对合意与非合意产出的贡献，并用收缩部分 $\\eta_j$ 表示仍属于投入组合的部分。凸性作用于完整活动账户，"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:135
#: 68de46e5821143ac8532092994a61f13
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathbf 1^\\top(\\mu+\\eta)=1,\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\mathbf 1^\\top(\\mu+\\eta)=1,\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:139
#: db69d7ce6dc4456b8628af28fcaa3d01
msgid ""
"while the activity-specific retention rate is $r_j=\\mu_j/(\\mu_j+\\eta_j)$ "
"whenever that activity has positive weight. This is a different economic "
"construction, not a cosmetic returns-to-scale switch. An equality such as "
"$B\\lambda=b$ without a coherent scaling or convexification account is "
"retained only as a legacy numerical formulation; it is not presented as a "
"named weak-disposal technology."
msgstr ""
"当活动权重为正时，活动特定保留率为 "
"$r_j=\\mu_j/(\\mu_j+\\eta_j)$。这是一种不同的经济构造，不是表面上的规模报酬开关。若没有连贯的缩放或凸化账户，$B\\lambda=b$"
" 这类等式只能保留为历史数值形式，不能作为具名弱可处置技术介绍。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:146
#: ce5845a3eb5c49d0be252f8b1ce6c8d0
msgid ""
"An equality alone does not identify weak disposal, whereas the CRS common-"
"factor construction uses one portfolio-wide retention rate and the VRS "
"activity-specific construction permits different retention rates across "
"reference activities"
msgstr "仅有一条等式不能识别弱可处置性；CRS 共同因子构造使用组合整体的一项保留率，而 VRS 活动特定构造允许参照活动具有不同保留率"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:151
#: 4a422f39426e4b1c8b8ed02379f6ca66
msgid ""
"The weak-disposal axiom admits more than one benchmarking construction. The "
"model must state how the reference activities are scaled before its "
"environmental comparison has a defensible production meaning."
msgstr "弱可处置公理允许不止一种标杆构造。模型必须说明参照活动如何缩放，环境比较才具有可辩护的生产含义。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:156
#: 7a08eff02d7345969fe16728ded5f272
msgid "The directional distance is a feasible management programme"
msgstr "方向性距离是一套可行管理改进方案"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:158
#: 63ca68116a1b42a4b0f2140c1b9634fd
msgid ""
"Environmental performance is not adequately summarized by “less pollution.” "
"The organization usually has obligations on several margins at once. Let "
"$g^x$, $g^y$, and $g^b$ be nonnegative quantities describing a proposed "
"reduction in inputs, an increase in desirable outputs, and a reduction in "
"undesirable outputs. Collect them as the declared environmental programme "
"$g=(g^x,g^y,g^b)$. The environmental directional distance is"
msgstr ""
"仅用“污染更少”不足以概括环境绩效。组织通常同时承担多方面责任。令非负数量 $g^x$、$g^y$ 和 $g^b$ "
"分别描述拟议的投入削减、合意产出增加与非合意产出减少，并把它们组成既定环境改进方案 $g=(g^x,g^y,g^b)$。环境方向性距离为"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:165
#: 1170a74b974f4d2c9f3575650d7d9228
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"D_{\\mathcal T}\n"
"(x_o,y_o,b_o;g)\n"
"=\\sup\\left\\{\n"
"\\beta:\n"
"(x_o-\\beta g^x,\n"
" y_o+\\beta g^y,\n"
" b_o-\\beta g^b)\n"
"\\in\\mathcal T\n"
"\\right\\}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"D_{\\mathcal T}\n"
"(x_o,y_o,b_o;g)\n"
"=\\sup\\left\\{\n"
"\\beta:\n"
"(x_o-\\beta g^x,\n"
" y_o+\\beta g^y,\n"
" b_o-\\beta g^b)\n"
"\\in\\mathcal T\n"
"\\right\\}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:177
#: 6dd0dca6c5ad43ce98f1c4eeff8acd11
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The resulting value $\\beta_o=D_{\\mathcal T}(x_o,y_o,b_o;g)$ is the largest"
" common ambition factor that the estimated technology can support. Its "
"operational content is $\\beta_o g$: the associated resource savings, "
"service expansion, and pollution reduction in the units managers actually "
"observe."
msgstr ""
"所得 $\\beta_o=D_{\\mathcal T}(x_o,y_o,b_o;g)$ 是估计技术能够支持的最大共同雄心水平。它的经营含义是 "
"$\\beta_o g$：用管理者实际观测的单位表示相应资源节约、服务扩张和污染削减。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:182
#: 40bbb3416f5148b994b3bc6e003e69ec
msgid "Different choices of $g$ pose different policy questions:"
msgstr "不同的 $g$ 选择提出不同的政策问题："

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:188
#: bb12af1fb34d4c9bb3889db97a440a1b
msgid "Programme"
msgstr "方案"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:189
#: af29a5c103914bda91df127070f6098e
msgid "Direction"
msgstr "方向"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:190
#: 6301192dbc72432dba909dc646c63861
msgid "Question posed"
msgstr "所提问题"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:191
#: 29199a1ecff84f3e869f1f1125b8da5e
msgid "Joint environmental improvement"
msgstr "联合环境改进"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:192
#: 32b237c79d194ed7ba2f1b8afb0a522c
msgid "$(0,y_o,b_o)$"
msgstr "$(0,y_o,b_o)$"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:193
#: 47466eccab3e43e4993ec37a03fba40d
msgid ""
"By what common proportion can desirable output rise and pollution fall with "
"the resource budget fixed?"
msgstr "资源预算固定时，合意产出可以增加、污染可以减少的共同百分比是多少？"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:195
#: 7270ad58cd00437dbb5d83b74bd19526
msgid "Service-expansion programme"
msgstr "服务扩张方案"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:196
#: 043ac1a42a4d439eb4324de032da719e
msgid "$(0,y_o,0)$"
msgstr "$(0,y_o,0)$"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:197
#: 1a1b1bfed8bb49b698a36f007c38cc9f
msgid ""
"How much desirable output can be added without requiring a pollution "
"reduction?"
msgstr "在不要求污染减少的情况下，可以增加多少合意产出？"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:199
#: 6d1683bfb93b4bda8f1e7bc5d86389d1
msgid "Pollution-control improvement"
msgstr "污染控制改进"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:200
#: 8c4a9a11d6ad4bcaad56de764d1e03f3
msgid "$(0,0,b_o)$"
msgstr "$(0,0,b_o)$"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:201
#: b3b825946fb548c69a05f6bea866fb50
msgid ""
"How much pollution can be reduced while resources and desirable output are "
"maintained?"
msgstr "资源和合意产出保持不变时，可以减少多少污染？"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:203
#: 63f49acb418b46f4881105320d5e5cbb
msgid "Resource–service–residual programme"
msgstr "资源—服务—残余物方案"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:204
#: eab55191583c42fd8f3099aab7be08f2
msgid "$(x_o,y_o,b_o)$"
msgstr "$(x_o,y_o,b_o)$"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:205
#: 9bc695e0771b4ea1af7693e869c7f9d5
msgid ""
"How ambitious can a coordinated conservation, expansion, and abatement plan "
"be?"
msgstr "协调的节约、扩张与治理方案可以达到多大幅度？"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:209
#: 5fd2916ff0df4aec99d1932feb29139b
msgid ""
"These are not alternative labels for the same score. They encode different "
"management commitments. A direction becomes a target only when it "
"corresponds to an institution's actual objectives and constraints. At least "
"one direction component must be strictly positive for every assessed "
"organization; an all-zero direction poses no improvement question and is "
"therefore undefined."
msgstr "这些不是同一个得分的不同名称，而是不同的管理承诺。只有方向符合机构真实目标与约束时，才可能进一步形成目标。对每个被评价组织，至少一个方向分量必须严格为正；全零方向没有提出改进问题，因此未定义。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:215
#: f0b9e64ebcdc4cbfa7b660b0fe2f7c21
msgid ""
"For the common-factor constant-returns technology, the joint-improvement "
"question is estimated from"
msgstr "对共同因子、规模报酬不变技术，联合改进问题通过下式估计："

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:218
#: 450d0e54955c4554ab879d2efac9f1b9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\max_{\\beta,\\lambda}\\quad &\\beta\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.}\\quad\n"
"&X\\lambda\\leq x_o-\\beta g^x,\\\\\n"
"&Y\\lambda\\geq y_o+\\beta g^y,\\\\\n"
"&B\\lambda=b_o-\\beta g^b,\\\\\n"
"&\\lambda\\geq0.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\max_{\\beta,\\lambda}\\quad &\\beta\\\\\n"
"\\text{约束条件}\\quad\n"
"&X\\lambda\\leq x_o-\\beta g^x,\\\\\n"
"&Y\\lambda\\geq y_o+\\beta g^y,\\\\\n"
"&B\\lambda=b_o-\\beta g^b,\\\\\n"
"&\\lambda\\geq0.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:229
#: 452ecef8ed3f4c228da0ab3f02a7b20d
msgid ""
"A positive $\\beta$ identifies an attainable directional plan relative to "
"the chosen reference evidence. A larger value means that more of the "
"declared improvement remains available; it is not “higher efficiency.” A "
"zero value means that this particular programme cannot be expanded further. "
"It establishes direction-specific efficiency, not necessarily "
"Pareto–Koopmans efficiency, because another mix of resource, service, or "
"residual changes may still be feasible."
msgstr ""
"正的 $\\beta$ 表示相对于所选参照证据存在可实现方向性方案。数值越大，表示既定改进仍有更多可用空间，而不是“效率越高”。取 0 "
"表示这项特定方案无法继续扩张，只能确立方向特定有效，未必达到 Pareto–Koopmans 有效，因为其他资源、服务或残余物变化组合仍可能可行。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:236
#: 7e6136ac33884bb48247281903adaf53
msgid ""
"When each organization belongs to its own reference set, the unchanged "
"observed plan is feasible and $\\beta\\geq0$. External reference sets "
"require more care. A signed negative distance can be retained when the "
"analyst explicitly requests it; otherwise the nonnegative programme is "
"reported as infeasible. For the equality-based common-factor technology, "
"even a positive directional target does not by itself prove that the "
"original assessed plan belongs to the external reference technology. DEAPack"
" therefore reports the native $\\beta$ whenever its programme is certified, "
"but releases the display transform $1/(1+\\beta)$, efficiency "
"classifications, and improvement plot only after reference-technology "
"membership is also certified."
msgstr ""
"当各组织属于自身参考集时，观测方案保持不变总是可行，因此 "
"$\\beta\\geq0$。使用外部参考集需要更谨慎：分析者明确请求时可以保留带符号负距离，否则把非负方案报告为不可行。对基于等式的共同因子技术，即使方向目标为正，也不能单独证明原被评价方案属于外部参照技术。因此，DEAPack"
" 在方案得到认证时报告原生 $\\beta$；只有参照技术成员资格也得到认证后，才发布展示变换 $1/(1+\\beta)$、效率分类和改进图。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:246
#: 5b0217dd82264b0a824c4cd7793b6175
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The first-stage directional plan is $({\\tilde x}_o,{\\tilde y}_o,{\\tilde "
"b}_o)= (x_o-\\beta g^x,y_o+\\beta g^y,b_o-\\beta g^b)$. A second stage may "
"complete that plan by removing input slack or adding desirable-output slack."
" Under strong disposal it may also remove residual slack; under common-"
"factor equality disposal the bad-output account remains fixed at ${\\tilde "
"b}_o$. We reserve hats for the completed target $({\\hat x}_o,{\\hat "
"y}_o,{\\hat b}_o)$."
msgstr ""
"第一阶段方向方案为 $({\\tilde x}_o,{\\tilde y}_o,{\\tilde b}_o)= (x_o-\\beta "
"g^x,y_o+\\beta g^y,b_o-\\beta "
"g^b)$。第二阶段可通过消除投入松弛或增加合意产出松弛来完成该方案。强可处置性下还可以消除残余物松弛；共同因子等式处置下，非合意产出账户固定在 "
"${\\tilde b}_o$。本书用帽号表示完成目标 $({\\hat x}_o,{\\hat y}_o,{\\hat b}_o)$。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:254
#: 755f0cf3fa9d4958a4e33b430642d578
msgid ""
"A regulator, hospital system, or utility may also have a legitimate reason "
"to limit who counts as a comparable operating peer: a common service "
"mandate, permit regime, or accounting boundary, for example. In the generic "
"DDF, common-factor weak-disposal DDF, and CFG preset, DEAPack lets the study"
" declare that comparison population explicitly. The declared rule is then "
"intersected with the chosen time/reference policy before the directional "
"programme is solved. This is a statement about admissible management "
"evidence, not a new pollution technology. It never turns strong disposal "
"into weak disposal, and it does not make a negative external CFG distance "
"disappear. The reported reference sizes and policy ledger should accompany "
"the distance wherever such a restriction is used."
msgstr ""
"监管者、医院系统或公用事业也可能有正当理由限制哪些组织可作为可比经营参照，例如共同服务使命、许可制度或会计边界。在通用 DDF、共同因子弱可处置 DDF"
" 和 CFG preset 中，DEAPack "
"允许研究明确声明比较总体。既定规则与所选时间/参照政策取交集后，再求解方向性方案。这是对合格管理证据的声明，不是新污染技术；它绝不会把强可处置性变成弱可处置性，也不会使负的外部"
" CFG 距离消失。使用这类限制时，报告距离应同时给出参照规模与政策记录。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:266
#: ed0deab462c24410b43ebc5ed179fb90
msgid "When one production relation hides the pollution mechanism"
msgstr "当一个生产关系掩盖污染机制"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:268
#: c66f3a5ce40a4d26a5c5e082aa55b6e9
msgid ""
"Weak and strong disposal describe what may happen inside one joint "
"technology. Some applications need to distinguish the activity that creates "
"desirable output from the physical relation that generates a residual. A "
"coal-fired plant, for example, draws on labour, capital, and fuel to produce"
" electricity, but the carbon content of its fuel has a special connection to"
" emissions. Treating every input as equally responsible for that residual "
"can obscure the environmental mechanism."
msgstr "弱、强可处置性描述一个联合技术内部允许发生什么。有些应用需要区分创造合意产出的活动与产生残余物的物理关系。例如，燃煤电厂利用劳动、资本和燃料生产电力，但燃料含碳量与排放具有特殊联系。把每项投入视为对残余物承担同样责任，可能掩盖环境机制。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:275
#: c51574a7863745859a7d686f394acb32
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The by-production approach represents the two relationships simultaneously "
"{cite:p}`murty2012`. Partition inputs as $x=(x^n,x^p)$, where $x^p$ contains"
" those inputs that physically generate the modeled residual. A common "
"empirical account is"
msgstr ""
"by-production 方法同时表示这两种关系 {cite:p}`murty2012`。把投入分为 $x=(x^n,x^p)$，其中 $x^p$ "
"包含会在物理上产生所建模残余物的投入。一种常见经验账户为"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:279
#: 23db73c81c584550b90eabd42b439750
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T_{BP}=\\mathcal T_1\\cap\\mathcal T_2,\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T_{BP}=\\mathcal T_1\\cap\\mathcal T_2,\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:283
#: 209ffe5d03eb42b580d557aabcbb2d0e
msgid "with intended production represented by"
msgstr "其中，预期生产关系表示为"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:285
#: c69fd98fd0e74d29a67b0241c3b7a84c
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T_1:\\qquad\n"
"X\\lambda\\le x,\\qquad Y\\lambda\\ge y,\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T_1:\\qquad\n"
"X\\lambda\\le x,\\qquad Y\\lambda\\ge y,\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:290
#: 2f15221740aa475f9168524cbac933f8
msgid "and residual generation represented by"
msgstr "残余物生成关系表示为"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:292
#: ba76525094e544eb8c8c046036f631f0
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T_2:\\qquad\n"
"X^p\\mu\\ge x^p,\\qquad B\\mu\\le b.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T_2:\\qquad\n"
"X^p\\mu\\ge x^p,\\qquad B\\mu\\le b.\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:297
#: 464a2d498ac142429a7041692ddbc30b
msgid ""
"Here $\\lambda,\\mu\\ge0$. As written, these are the constant-returns "
"relations used in the classical source account. The inequality $B\\mu\\le b$"
" should not be read in isolation as ordinary free disposal. Together with "
"$X^p\\mu\\ge x^p$, it says that reducing the represented residual cannot be "
"separated from the inputs that generate it. This is *costly disposal inside "
"the residual-generation relation*: an opportunity-set restriction, not a "
"monetary cost, an observed treatment process, or an engineering abatement "
"technology."
msgstr ""
"这里 $\\lambda,\\mu\\ge0$。所写关系是经典来源账户采用的规模报酬不变形式。不能把不等式 $B\\mu\\le b$ "
"单独理解为普通自由处置性；与 $X^p\\mu\\ge x^p$ "
"结合后，它表示所代表残余物的减少不能与产生残余物的投入分离。这是**残余物生成关系内部的有成本处置**：一项机会集限制，而不是货币成本、观测处理过程或工程治理技术。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:305
#: cfbdc04b6edf4225b2e62a2ce4bfa992
msgid ""
"The two reference combinations are deliberately distinct. An electricity "
"producer may learn about production capacity from one set of plants and "
"about the emissions associated with fuel use from another. The observed plan"
" must nevertheless pass both relations."
msgstr "两套参照组合有意保持不同。发电企业可以从一组电厂学习生产能力，同时从另一组电厂了解燃料使用相关排放；但观测方案必须同时满足两种关系。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:310
#: d20c2a990ff840309e2a8e63d100fc92
msgid ""
"By-production intersects an intended-production relation with a residual-"
"generation relation using separate reference combinations"
msgstr "by-production 把预期生产关系与残余物生成关系相交，并使用不同参照组合"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:315
#: 81335c95dba149bfb19e04f964f6321d
msgid ""
"By-production separates the intended-production account from the residual-"
"generation account while requiring the organization to satisfy both."
msgstr "by-production 在要求组织同时满足两类关系的同时，把预期生产账户与残余物生成账户分开。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:319
#: 70cf01f9c5534ee997f3e78f8272dfa4
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The conventional BP-DDF implemented here holds ordinary inputs fixed and "
"declares $g^{BP}=(0,g^y,g^b)$. On the same directional scale, its two "
"accounts ask for"
msgstr "本章实现的传统 BP-DDF 保持普通投入不变，并声明 $g^{BP}=(0,g^y,g^b)$。在同一方向尺度上，两个账户分别考察"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:322
#: 5c701f4129bf42ad8dfba097be5a6d07
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\beta_o^1&=\\sup\\{\\beta:X\\lambda\\le x_o,\\ \n"
"Y\\lambda\\ge y_o+\\beta g^y\\},\\\\\n"
"\\beta_o^2&=\\sup\\{\\beta:X^p\\mu\\ge x_o^p,\\ \n"
"B\\mu\\le b_o-\\beta g^b\\}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\beta_o^1&=\\sup\\{\\beta:X\\lambda\\le x_o,\\ \n"
"Y\\lambda\\ge y_o+\\beta g^y\\},\\\\\n"
"\\beta_o^2&=\\sup\\{\\beta:X^p\\mu\\ge x_o^p,\\ \n"
"B\\mu\\le b_o-\\beta g^b\\}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:331
#: 060d0d4d7d0f4b96914cd22ea6582b84
msgid ""
"The classical source profile holds the nonnegative output and residual "
"directions fixed across the compared organizations. Thus $\\beta_o^1$ and "
"$\\beta_o^2$ are commensurable ambitions, not distances computed under two "
"unrelated management programmes. A common programme constrained by both "
"accounts has"
msgstr ""
"经典来源设定在被比较组织之间保持非负产出和残余物方向不变。因此，$\\beta_o^1$ 与 $\\beta_o^2$ "
"是可比较的改进幅度，不是在两套互不相干的管理方案下计算的距离。同时受两个账户约束的共同方案满足"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:336
#: cb6c9d64eb5a4ce994478fdf3671d58a
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\beta_o^{BP}=\\min\\{\\beta_o^1,\\beta_o^2\\}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\beta_o^{BP}=\\min\\{\\beta_o^1,\\beta_o^2\\}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:340
#: 1f3b24fb6a1441f38e8faf6b914f9e9e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Both direction blocks must pose a substantive question: at least one "
"desirable-output direction component must be positive and at least one "
"residual direction component must be positive. The minimum also creates an "
"important interpretive limit. If $\\beta_o^{BP}=0$, only one component "
"account needs to be at its directional limit; the other may still contain "
"substantial improvement potential. Zero therefore does not establish "
"componentwise efficiency, and still less strong efficiency of the whole "
"operation."
msgstr ""
"两个方向块都必须提出实质问题：至少一个合意产出方向分量为正，至少一个残余物方向分量为正。取最小值还带来重要解释限制。若 "
"$\\beta_o^{BP}=0$，只需一个分量账户达到其方向极限，另一个仍可能有大量改进空间。因此，零值不能确立分量逐项有效，更不能确立整个经营活动强有效。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:348
#: 4a54fa3d78f2445187d814b4caff6d24
msgid ""
"The smaller component is the *direction-specific limiting account*. "
"Reporting both components shows whether the intended-production relation or "
"the residual-generation relation limits this declared common programme. It "
"does not, by itself, identify a physical bottleneck, a causal management "
"constraint, or an emissions-control process. That interpretation depends on "
"identifying $x^p$ from scientific or engineering knowledge; a statistical "
"column name cannot establish which inputs physically generate a residual."
msgstr ""
"较小分量是**方向特定的限制账户**。同时报告两个分量，可说明在这套共同方案中是预期生产关系还是残余物生成关系限制改进。但它本身不能识别物理瓶颈、因果管理约束或排放控制过程。相关解释依赖科学或工程知识识别"
" $x^p$；一个统计列名无法证明哪些投入在物理上产生残余物。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:356
#: f8b94b3965f84f45b22307f5d763d416
msgid ""
"Because the conclusion depends on the intersection of two production "
"relations, both accounts must reproduce their quantity commitments before "
"the common distance, target, or peer comparison has an economic "
"interpretation. If either account cannot be reconstructed, the evidence is "
"insufficient to support the joint environmental conclusion. Satisfying both "
"accounts still does not turn the directional target into a strongly "
"efficient engineering design. By-production remains a useful alternative "
"production account within environmental directional analysis, not a "
"universally preferable pollution score, a chemical mass-balance model, or a "
"detailed account of capture, treatment, and recycling."
msgstr ""
"由于结论依赖两个生产关系的交集，在共同距离、目标或参照单元比较获得经济含义前，两个账户都必须重构其数量承诺。任一账户无法重构时，证据不足以支持联合环境结论。即使两个账户均满足，也不会把方向目标变成强有效工程设计"
"。by-production 仍是环境方向性分析中的一种替代生产账户，而不是普遍更优的污染得分、化学质量平衡模型或捕集、处理与回收的详细模型。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:366
#: 494cbfe506bc41e6a7fc23a35e20b924
msgid "Reading the two accounts in practice"
msgstr "在实践中解读两个账户"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:368
#: d628aa1d8f5047f1bd445d2d0f926da4
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The five-organization teaching example from Murty, Russell, and Levkoff "
"makes the minimum rule visible without adding another model family "
"{cite:p}`murty2012`:"
msgstr "Murty、Russell 和 Levkoff 的五组织教学案例无需再增加模型族，就能清楚展示最小值规则 {cite:p}`murty2012`："

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:394
#: 671690fdcc9e4fd8a99f22d61118cc02
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For DMU 3, the intended-production account supports $\\beta^1=4/3$, while "
"the residual-generation account supports $\\beta^2=1$. The joint programme "
"is therefore limited by the residual-generation relation and "
"$\\beta^{BP}=1$. Starting from $(x^p,y,b)=(1,2/3,2)$, the common directional"
" target is $(1,5/3,1)$. The intended account alone could support $y=2$, but "
"that endpoint is not the joint operating plan. The peer tables make the "
"separation equally concrete: DMU 1 supports the intended-production account,"
" whereas DMU 2 supports the residual account. This is exactly why the two "
"component distances and two peer systems should accompany the minimum rather"
" than disappear behind one headline number."
msgstr ""
"对 DMU 3，预期生产账户支持 $\\beta^1=4/3$，残余物生成账户支持 "
"$\\beta^2=1$，所以联合方案受残余物生成关系限制，$\\beta^{BP}=1$。从 $(x^p,y,b)=(1,2/3,2)$ "
"出发，共同方向目标为 $(1,5/3,1)$。单独的预期生产账户可以支持 $y=2$，但该端点不是联合经营方案。参照单元表同样直观：DMU 1 "
"支持预期生产账户，DMU 2 支持残余物账户。这正说明为什么应同时报告两个分量距离和两套参照系统，而不能让它们消失在一个核心数值之后。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:405
#: 47e27aa2fdfb42fea13c6ac96d0a973b
msgid "From environmental performance to productivity change"
msgstr "从环境绩效到生产率变化"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:407
#: ca1f154b1ae64a928189417c6d5fdcd3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Evaluating an operation against another period's technology can produce a "
"signed cross-technology distance, but one such comparison is not itself a "
"productivity index. Part IV develops the required combinations of "
"contemporaneous and cross-period environmental distances in "
"{doc}`../04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference`."
msgstr ""
"把经营活动放到另一时期技术下评价可能产生带符号跨技术距离，但一次比较本身不是生产率指数。第四部分在 {doc}`../04-productivity"
"/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference` 中组合必要的同期与跨期环境距离。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:413
#: 375f4b72063248afb034a1e8faa99212
msgid "A contemporaneous power-plant comparison"
msgstr "一个同期发电企业比较"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:415
#: 7c5061c3cc734d8eb9d771624f3e5646
msgid ""
"The `environmental_panel` teaching data contain energy, labour, electricity,"
" and carbon dioxide for several plants over four periods. Suppose the "
"immediate management question is: with each plant's current energy and "
"labour commitment, how much can electricity rise while carbon dioxide falls "
"in the same proportion? A contemporaneous reference means that each plant is"
" compared with operating practices observed in its own year."
msgstr ""
"`environmental_panel` "
"教学数据包含若干电厂四个时期的能源、劳动、电力和二氧化碳。设当前管理问题为：在各电厂现有能源与劳动承诺下，电力增加与二氧化碳减少可以达到多大共同比例？同期参照表示每家电厂只与本年度观测经营实践比较。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:443
#: 74ff6628c98740aab7f1997fa7e4659d
msgid "The fitted account can display the supported variable-level plan directly:"
msgstr "拟合账户可以直接展示各变量得到支持的方案："

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:455
#: 9be51094d5e54efa9aca8a7c58495e31
msgid ""
"Writing the directions explicitly keeps the economic promise visible: "
"ordinary inputs are protected, desirable electricity expands in proportion "
"to its observed level, and undesirable carbon dioxide contracts in "
"proportion to its observed level. The technology is the family-level CRS "
"common-factor weak- disposal account introduced above; a historical source "
"label is not needed to define another model."
msgstr ""
"明确写出方向，可以让经济承诺保持可见：普通投入受到保护，合意电力按观测水平同比例扩张，非合意二氧化碳按观测水平同比例收缩。技术采用上文介绍的模型族层面 "
"CRS 共同因子弱可处置账户，不需要另用历史来源标签定义一个新模型。"

#: ../../chapters/03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-ddf.md:462
#: 5742c7931b0941e1820cfb75bc28ee45
msgid ""
"For Central in 2020, $\\beta=0.083815$. Conditional on the observed "
"comparison group and the common-factor constant-returns technology, its "
"resource commitment supports a coordinated plan with approximately 8.38 "
"percent more electricity and 8.38 percent less carbon dioxide."
msgstr ""
"对 2020 年 "
"Central，$\\beta=0.083815$。以观测比较群体和共同因子规模报酬不变技术为条件，其资源承诺支持一项协调方案：电力约增加 "
"8.38%，二氧化碳约减少 8.38%。"

